<DocumentLayout
  title="Progress & plans"
  description="What works in Locus today, what is planned, and what is still being explored."
>
  <h1>Built a little at a time.</h1>
  <p>
    The aim is a calm, practical space for studying books and papers. This page separates what works
    now from what is still an idea. Plans are not delivery promises.
  </p>
  <h2>Working now</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Workspaces and folders that reference existing PDFs.</li>
    <li>Continuous PDF reading with saved positions, document links, and zoom controls.</li>
    <li>Excalidraw whiteboards with local saving.</li>
    <li>Up to four resizable panes for reading and drawing.</li>
    <li>A command palette, configurable keyboard shortcuts, and light/dark themes.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Being prepared</h2>
  <p>
    A repeatable local Debian build, clearer release notes, and this public guide. These support
    testing and feedback before a public installer is offered.
  </p>
  <h2>Planned</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Drop a pin at a location in a PDF and attach a drawing to it.</li>
    <li>Keep several drawings for the same book, section, or exercise.</li>
    <li>Create and connect Markdown notes alongside handwritten work.</li>
    <li>Choose where notes and drawings are stored.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Still being explored</h2>
  <p>
    Connections across study materials, additional installer formats, and optional assistance using
    selected context. Independent study will not require AI.
  </p>
  <h2>Follow the actual changes</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a> records completed, user-visible changes.
    <a href="https://github.com/HYP3R00T/Locus/issues">GitHub issues</a>
    are the place to discuss problems and suggestions.
  </p>
</DocumentLayout>
